WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.277
Let’s apply that conversion pattern.

00:00:02.277 --> 00:00:09.952
Price begins as the text “29.99” and quantity begins as the text “5”.

00:00:09.952 --> 00:00:12.522
Float converts the price to a decimal number.

00:00:12.522 --> 00:00:17.652
Int converts the quantity to a whole number.

00:00:17.652 --> 00:00:20.232
Now Python can multiply them.

00:00:20.232 --> 00:00:28.378
Twenty-nine dollars and ninety-nine cents times five gives one hundred forty-nine dollars and ninety-five cents.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:31.960
The final f-string formats that number as money.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:38.015
Change the quantity from five to eight, predict the new total, and then run the code.

00:00:38.015 --> 00:00:40.934
This is a very typical data-cleaning step.
